10. Performance, SEO and Accessibility

This is a visually advanced website, but it must work on ordinary phones and slower connections in Bangladesh.

Performance targets:

- Aim for strong Core Web Vitals: LCP at or below 2.5 seconds, INP at or below 200 milliseconds, and CLS at or below 0.1 under Google's recommended assessment conditions.
- Optimize the initial hero and avoid unnecessary JavaScript.
- Use properly sized responsive images and modern image formats.
- Lazy-load below-the-fold media.
- Use thumbnails and compressed models for interactive 3D.
- Avoid downloading full video backgrounds before they are needed.
- Preserve responsive layouts and prevent layout shifts.
- Prefer real performance testing over claims about a score.

Accessibility:

- Semantic HTML.
- Keyboard-operable navigation, galleries and diagrams.
- Visible focus states.
- Accessible form labels and validation messages.
- Sufficient color contrast.
- Alt text for meaningful images.
- Captions or transcripts for important video content.
- Reduced-motion support.
- Text alternatives for essential 3D interactions.

SEO:

- Unique title and meta description for each page.
- Open Graph metadata.
- Canonical URLs after the domain is confirmed.
- XML sitemap and robots configuration.
- Appropriate structured data where the actual business facts justify it.
- Descriptive URLs.
- Optimized Bengali and English metadata where useful.
- No fabricated address, opening hours, phone number, certification, review or rating structured data.

